A circle of radius 1 is tangent to a circle of radius X. The sides of $\triangle ABC$ are tangent to the circles as shown, and the sides $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{AC}$ are congruent. What is the area of $\triangle ABC$?

[asy]
unitsize(0.7cm);
pair A,B,C;
A=(0,8);
B=(-2.8,0);
C=(2.8,0);
draw(A--B--C--cycle,linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle((0,2),2),linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle((0,5),1),linewidth(0.7));
draw((0,2)--(2,2));
draw((0,5)--(1,5));
label("2",(1,2),N);
label("1",(0.5,5),N);
label("$A$",A,N);
label("$B$",B,SW);
label("$C$",C,SE);
[/asy]
